  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Role and Character
    
    Angmo xang'Oath holds the rank of Senior Assessor within E'frostlings, the Aurora Stack trade faction, operating from E'frostlings Central Holdings. She receives commercial reconnaissance from field bureaus — the 4th Terrace Bureau's vulnerability profile on the Shadow Covens' extraction operations at ☽'shadow Umbrsulcavus~ is one documented example — and acts on that intelligence with a directness her counterparts have learned not to mistake for impulsiveness.
    
    Her flippers bear the fine-scribed tattoos of a contract-keeper, every brokered deal marked into the skin. Her left flipper trembles during high-stakes negotiations, a tell she has never fully suppressed; whether it signals triumph or fear depends on what she has just agreed to. She carries herself with the studied casualness of someone who spent the Faction Wars grinding rivals into ice-dust and wants every room to remember it. She broke three guild compacts in a single season during E'frostlings' expansion — a figure I have not been able to independently verify, though no one has disputed it either, which in commercial circles amounts to the same thing.
    
    ## Territorial Expansion
    
    Angmo led the E'frostlings delegation to The Hearth Plaza, the Aurora Stack's central council chamber, following her faction's conquest of The Veil Vents. She claimed authority over territory formerly held by the Shadow Covens and Threshold, a rival faction, along with twelve guilds that had depended on both. She demanded recalculation of fire-core allocations across the Flipper Accord and presented updated trade-maps for the registry, framing E'frostlings' seizures as notifications rather than petitions.
    
    She noted that E'frostlings jointly held the Directrix Mirror — a ceremonial artifact used to authenticate territorial transfers — with the Icebound Exchange, the Aurora Stack's nominal governing body, and let the word *jointly* carry the weight of a deadline.
    
    ## The Foedus∴vincu
    
    When Light-Regent Xouhoulong, then head of the Hearth Plaza council, produced the Foedus∴vincu — a compact granting the orca raiders known as the Midnight Claws diplomatic passage through the Berg's deep routes — Angmo recognized the danger but agreed to witness the sealing. She insisted E'frostlings provide two of the required witnesses, non-negotiable, and demanded copies of every document.
    
    The compact was sealed. The Calving followed shortly after, killing many. Xouhoulong resigned. Angmo's witnesses survived. Her copies, presumably, remain in E'frostlings Central Holdings. She had said the ice would remember who held the seal. She made certain of it.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771593532194_0", anchor: "following her faction's conquest of The Veil Vents", text: "A corruption breach-point. One of the Berg's active source zones — cold-burn discoloration, whisper-echoes, the full catalogue. E'frostlings marched into a wound in the ice and presented it to the Hearth Plaza as a commercial acquisition. Not a single councilor asked what, precisely, they now owned. The updated trade-maps would have shown extraction routes threading through corruption-scarred territory, and the twelve guilds Angmo claimed were guilds that had been operating adjacent to a breach for years. She conquered a disease and invoiced it as real estate. Magnificent, really.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771593532194_1", anchor: "a figure I have not been able to independently verify", text: "Nor will I be. E'frostlings' internal compact registry is sealed under guild-privilege, and my requests were declined with a politeness that made the refusal worse. The hedge in the main text is doing all the work here. Angmo's reputation is built partly on numbers no one can check — a strategy I recognize because the Nightshelf perfected it centuries earlier.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771593532194_2", anchor: "jointly held the Directrix Mirror", text: "Three entries now where this instrument appears at a moment of authentication it should not be trusted to perform. The Mirror is damaged — the world dynamics index lists it among artifacts awaiting restoration or destruction. Angmo let the word *jointly* carry a threat, but the object she was threatening with is cracked. Either she didn't know, or — funnier — she did, and was betting the Exchange didn't.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771593532194_3", anchor: "She had said the ice would remember who held the seal", text: "It does. Stratum 4 preserves the thermal signatures of all parties present. Angmo's witnesses survived the Calving; her copies survived Xouhoulong's resignation. She walked into a room, watched a catastrophe get authorized, and left holding the receipts. Contract-keeper to the bone.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
